><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k \\in A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a_1, \\ldots, a_k \\in A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7335em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span>. Can anyone recall which paper it was?</p>","timestamp":1722496139,"subject":"a recent preprint on operations with restricted arities","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":116664,"sender_id":1037,"sender_full_name":"J-B Vienney","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/04c19b4b544f7d2de22328021eb01278?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/a.20recent.20preprint.20on.20operations.20with.20restricted.20arities/near/116664\">#2</a> Maybe you are thinking about my talk at FMCS 2024. I talk about the set of arities on slide 4. <a href=\"https://pages.cpsc.ucalgary.ca/~robin/FMCS/FMCS2024/slides/FMCS2024-Vienney.pdf\">slides</a>. We talked quite a bit about this on Zulip. There is no preprint today because I thought that the notion wasn’t yet enough general and is probably included into an existing notion. But maybe I should try to write one if there is some interest about this notion.</p>","timestamp":1722599171,"subject":"a recent preprint on operations with restricted arities","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":116674,"sender_id":1037,"sender_full_name":"J-B Vienney","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/04c19b4b544f7d2de22328021eb01278?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/a.20recent.20preprint.20on.20operations.20with.20restricted.20arities/near/116674\">#3</a> Let me know if this is not what you were thinking about. If there is a preprint as you said, then it is quite intriguing to me.</p>","timestamp":1722620359,"subject":"a recent preprint on operations with restricted arities","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":116691,"sender_id":216,"sender_full_name":"Karol Szumiło","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0aca24940ce848fd62418e87ff4a2f3a?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/a.20recent.20preprint.20on.20operations.20with.20restricted.20arities/near/116691\">#4</a> The definition on your slide 4 is indeed the one that I was asking about. However, I haven’t seen your talk and I’m pretty sure I haven’t seen your slides until now either. I must have seen this notion in an arXiv paper not too long ago.</p>","timestamp":1722698805,"subject":"a recent preprint on operations with restricted arities","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]